course: dictionary
lesson: 15637
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning is right. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «We waited in the airport terminal for two hours.» A terminal here is a big building where journeys start or end. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A building fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «Connect the red wire to the positive terminal of the battery.» Now terminal means one of the metal ends where a wire joins. The words wire and battery are the clues. Always test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: Terminal is a word with several meanings, so check the context before you decide.
fact: A terminal can be a big building at an airport, bus station, train station or port where journeys start or end.
fact: A terminal can be one of the metal ends of a battery where wires are joined, such as the positive and negative terminals.
fact: On a computer, a terminal is a screen and keyboard used to work with the computer, or a program for typing commands.
fact: Terminal also means at the end, as in «terminal station», and a terminal illness is one that cannot be cured.
exercise: «We waited an hour in the airport terminal for our flight.» What is a terminal in this sentence? | A kind of illness | A screen and keyboard for a computer | A metal end of a battery | *A big building where journeys start or end
exercise: «Connect the wire to the negative terminal of the battery.» What is a terminal in this sentence? | *A metal end where a wire joins a battery | A long, narrow road | A place to buy train tickets | A computer program for typing commands
exercise: «Type the command into the terminal to open the folder.» What is a terminal in this sentence? | *A screen and keyboard for working with a computer | A kind of tree | A metal end of a battery | A bus or train station
test: «The bus left from the terminal at nine o'clock.» What does terminal mean here? | A sad illness that cannot be cured | A metal end where wires join | A computer program | *A big building where buses and journeys start or end
test: What does terminal mean in the phrase «terminal station»? | Covered in metal | At the start, before any trains leave | *At the end | Very dangerous
exam: Which clue shows that terminal means a battery end in «Connect the red wire to the positive terminal of the battery.»? | The word red on its own | Nothing, it is only a guess | *The words wire and battery | The word Connect on its own
